      "Frame 5: robot_01 extends its screen-right arm farther across the upper-middle face of rack_01 while its other arm stays bent nearer the head and chest. The extended gripper is close to the rack's right vertical side, above cable_02\u2013cable_04; the shoulders and head remain oriented toward the rack. Its base sits slightly farther left than before, creating a diagonal reach. server_01 stays horizontal on table_01, with cable_01 still coiled at the rear-right corner. table_02 remains empty, and server_02 cannot yet be isolated visually from the rack equipment. tray_01, keyboard_01, and mouse_01 remain partly obscured below the arms. rack_02 and power_strip_01 are unchanged at the right edge. shelf_01 retains computer_01\u2013computer_04 above, computer_05\u2013computer_07 in the middle, and computer_08\u2013computer_10 below. shelf_02 retains computer_11\u2013computer_13 above, computer_14 in the middle, and computer_15\u2013computer_17 below. monitor_01, monitor_02, and cabinet_01 remain stationary, with both monitor screens dark.",
      "Frame 6: robot_01 draws the previously extended arm inward and lowers both hands slightly toward the rack's colored-cable level. Its elbows remain bent and raised, and its torso remains upright, facing rack_01 at close arm's reach. The head is directed toward the space between the grippers and the rack. server_01 remains untouched on table_01; cable_01 remains coiled on the same table. table_02 is empty. server_02 is still not separately visible. cable_02, cable_03, and cable_04 retain their positions, with the robot's hands nearby but no clearly resolved change to their routing. tray_01, keyboard_01, and mouse_01 remain lower down and partly hidden. rack_02 and power_strip_01 remain cropped at far right. shelf_01 and computer_01\u2013computer_10, and shelf_02 and computer_11\u2013computer_17, are stationary in their original shelf groupings. monitor_01 and monitor_02 stay dark; cabinet_01 remains in place.",
