      "Frame 2: Robot_01 is now bent down toward the loose components on the left tabletop. Gripper_01 is close to the surface, immediately over a small yellow piece to the left of part_01; its fingers nearly reach the piece. Part_01 rests as a large round component below-right of the gripper, part_02 lies farther forward, and part_04 stands on an edge to their right. Part_05 lies diagonally between the circular components. The long and short yellow pins, part_06\u2013part_08, and small pieces part_09\u2013part_10 are dispersed around this cluster and toward the board; part_03 appears as a small cylinder near the robot base. Board_01 and all six gray fixtures remain stationary and visibly unoccupied by the major yellow components. The gripper is roughly two gripper widths left of the board's rear-left region.",
      "Frame 3: Robot_01 has swept rightward over board_01 and rotated its wrist so that gripper_01 slopes down toward the right. A slender yellow component, consistent with part_08 in the following placement, protrudes below the fingertips. The fingers hover above the board's right half, still separated from fixture_06 by a visible gap. Fixture_01, fixture_02, fixture_03, and holders fixture_04\u2013fixture_06 remain exposed. On table_01 to the left, part_01, part_02, part_04, and part_05 retain their loose arrangement. Part_03 remains near the robot base. Part_06, part_07, part_09, and part_10 remain among the scattered small yellow pieces beside and behind the board. The camera and board orientation are unchanged.",
