      "Frame 17: humanoid_robot_1 continues the half-kneel, shifting its torso slightly over the planted image-right foot. Its opposite knee remains down and its rear foot is angled upward behind the body. Both arms extend forward with a small gap between the hands. The torso-to-polished_floor_1 distance increases slightly, but knee contact remains visible. robot_beanie_1 stays on the head; robot_lanyard_1 and robot_identification_badge_1 hang forward. living_plant_wall_1, staircase_1, and stair_handrail_1 remain behind it. reception_counter_1, backpack_1, orchid_arrangement_1, and the seated people at right remain separated by several meters, with no interaction. chair_1\u2013chair_8, table_1\u2013table_4, standing_sign_1\u2013standing_sign_2, and display_screen_1 remain mostly offscreen to the left. support_column_1\u2013support_column_4, overhead_slatted_structure_1, and upper_level_railing_1 retain their positions. Background members of person_1\u2013person_15 include the stair-side standing person and a walker crossing the rear, but complete identity tracking is unavailable.",
      "Frame 18: humanoid_robot_1 maintains the wide half-kneeling configuration and rotates its upper body subtly toward image right. The planted foot stays flat, the opposite knee stays against polished_floor_1, and the hands remain suspended forward of the waist. robot_beanie_1 is unchanged; robot_lanyard_1 and robot_identification_badge_1 move slightly off-center with the torso. living_plant_wall_1 remains the dominant rear surface, and staircase_1 with stair_handrail_1 stays behind and to the right. The robot does not visibly approach reception_counter_1, backpack_1, orchid_arrangement_1, or the seated reception-side observers. The chair_1\u2013chair_8 and table_1\u2013table_4 cluster remains largely outside the crop, with standing_sign_1\u2013standing_sign_2 and display_screen_1 unresolved. Visible support_column_1\u2013support_column_4 portions, overhead_slatted_structure_1, and upper_level_railing_1 remain static. A background pedestrian progresses along the plant-wall side; the remaining requested person_1\u2013person_15 labels cannot be reliably matched to individual bodies.",
