      "Frame 28: The robot holds its near hand against the same upper-left control area with only a small wrist adjustment. Its torso stays upright beside the counter, and the farther arm remains bent low. The black-capped head continues facing the machine. The near hand is at contact distance from the panel, while the cup remains several hand-widths lower on the drip tray. The portafilter is still attached, its handle horizontal to the left, and the black hopper remains unchanged above. The tamper is not clearly visible. The steel milk pitcher and large potted plant remain stationary to the right on the wooden counter. Cabinets, stove, range hood, sink, faucet, dishwasher, window and blind, shelves of drinking glasses and dishes, toaster, countertop storage containers, sink-side bottles, small potted plant, and both framed artworks retain their positions. No distinct liquid flow or cup-level change is resolved.",
      "Frame 29: The robot withdraws its near hand from the machine's controls and lowers it toward waist height. The elbow opens slightly as the hand moves left, increasing its distance from the front panel. The farther hand remains near the lower torso, and the black-capped head tips down toward the cup. The reddish espresso cup remains upright beneath the dispensing head on the slotted drip tray. The portafilter stays attached with its handle projecting left; the hopper remains on top, and the tamper is not separately visible. The milk pitcher and large plant remain motionless to the right. The wooden countertop, cabinets, stove, range hood, sink, faucet, dishwasher, bright window and blind, wall shelves, glasses, dishes, toaster, storage containers, sink bottles, small plant, and framed artworks remain fixed. Both hands are now outside the machine's control and dispensing areas.",
