      "Frame 7: robot_1 begins moving the near gripper leftward and slightly upward with both wine glasses enclosed together. wine_glass_1 and wine_glass_2 remain almost parallel, with their bowls immediately next to each other. Their stems and feet are partly hidden below the hand; the right foot is close to the table but appears to begin separating from it. The forearm stays horizontal over dining_table_1, with the elbow toward the left edge. dinner_plate_1, salad_1, placemat_1, fork_1, and knife_1 remain beneath and behind the moving arm without visible contact. dining_chair_1 is unchanged. placemat_2, placemat_3, and the cropped dinner_plate_2 remain at the right side of the composition. napkin_1 is obscured or indistinct, and the spoon, divided dish, food pieces, mug, shakers, and farther dining chairs are not shown. Upper and lower kitchen cabinets and wooden worktops remain softly focused in the background. No state is observable for dishwasher_1, dishwasher_door_1, dishwasher_upper_rack_1, or dishwasher_lower_rack_1. The other listed appliances and accessories are outside the crop or too blurred for individual assessment. The glasses now move together rather than remaining separated between hand and table.",
      "Frame 8: robot_1 retracts the near arm slightly toward its body and raises the paired glasses. wine_glass_1 leans a little left, while wine_glass_2 remains closer to upright; their bowls overlap in the image. Their feet are now visibly close together beneath the gripper, with increasing clearance above dining_table_1. The hand is no longer centered over dinner_plate_1 but nearer the table's right-hand place-setting boundary. dinner_plate_1 and salad_1 remain undisturbed on placemat_1, with fork_1 and knife_1 near the plate. dining_chair_1, placemat_2, placemat_3, and the partially cropped dinner_plate_2 stay fixed. napkin_1 remains indistinct. divided_serving_dish_1, food_pieces_1, spoon_1, blue_mug_1, both dark shakers, and dining_chair_2 and dining_chair_3 are not visible. The kitchen background remains blurred cabinetry and counters, without a clearly readable change in any appliance. dishwasher_1 and its door and racks are outside the view, as are reliable details of refrigerator_1, oven_1, stovetop_1, range_hood_1, cookware, kitchen_island_1, shelves, plants, bottles, coffee_machine_1, framed_picture_1, and kitchen_door_1. The gripper-to-glass distance is zero at the visible holding surfaces.",
      "Frame 9: robot_1 lifts both wine_glass_1 and wine_glass_2 clearly above dining_table_1. The two circular feet hang beneath the gripper, with a visible gap of approximately a glass-foot diameter or more above the tabletop. The near elbow bends, bringing the hand inward and upward; the paired bowls remain close together. dinner_plate_1, salad_1, fork_1, and knife_1 stay on placemat_1 below. dining_chair_1 is visible behind the near table edge. A folded light napkin_1 becomes clearer behind the salad plate. placemat_2 and a portion of dinner_plate_2 remain at the right; placemat_3 is partly cropped near the camera. divided_serving_dish_1, food_pieces_1, spoon_1, blue_mug_1, dark_shaker_1, dark_shaker_2, dining_chair_2, and dining_chair_3 are not yet clearly shown. The rising framing exposes more pale kitchen cabinetry and wood counters, but fine accessory identities remain indistinct. dishwasher_1, dishwasher_door_1, both racks, and refrigerator_1 are outside this view. Oven, stovetop, hood, cookware, knife block, cutting boards, utensil holder, plants, bottles, shelves, coffee machine, framed picture, and kitchen door are not reliably assessable from this close angle.",
      "Frame 10: robot_1 holds wine_glass_1 and wine_glass_2 together at approximately lower-torso height, well clear of dining_table_1. Its elbow is bent and the near forearm slopes upward toward the paired glasses. The glasses remain apparently empty, with upright bowls and their feet hanging below the closed gripper. The lower portion of the robot's white torso and dark trim enters the frame, while the table and dining_chair_1 recede to the bottom edge. dinner_plate_1, salad_1, placemat_1, fork_1, knife_1, and napkin_1 are now mostly below the crop. Portions of the other placemats and dinner_plate_2 are likewise cut off. The blue mug, divided serving dish, food pieces, spoon, shakers, and farther chairs are not visible. Pale upper_kitchen_cabinets_1 and lower_kitchen_cabinets_1 and wooden kitchen counters fill more of the background, but their small contents remain out of focus. dishwasher_1, dishwasher_door_1, dishwasher_upper_rack_1, dishwasher_lower_rack_1, refrigerator_1, oven_1, stovetop_1, and range_hood_1 are not sufficiently visible here. No contact occurs between the suspended glass feet and any table object; the nearest visible surfaces are substantially below the hand.",
      "Frame 11: The camera changes to a frontal medium view of robot_1 behind dining_table_1. Its right hand, on the image left, holds wine_glass_1 and wine_glass_2 together near waist height; the bowls lean slightly apart while their stems are gathered in the gripper. Its left arm extends downward toward blue_mug_1 on the image right, with the open fingers close to the mug's side. The robot's white head has two dark vertical eye-like marks and a dark cap; its torso is mounted on a narrow vertical support. divided_serving_dish_1 sits on placemat_2 with food_pieces_1 in one compartment, and spoon_1 lies nearby. dark_shaker_1 and dark_shaker_2 stand near the foreground-right edge. dinner_plate_1 with salad_1 and the associated fork, knife, napkin, and placemat are partly cropped at the left; dinner_plate_2 and placemat_3 are only partially represented. dining_chair_2 and dining_chair_3 are behind the table on the right. Background upper and lower cabinets, wooden counters, microwave_1, kitchen_island_1, and kitchen_door_1 are visible. Other small kitchen accessories are indistinct. dishwasher_1, its door and racks, refrigerator_1, and the robot's base are outside this view.",
      "Frame 12: robot_1 keeps both wine glasses suspended in its right hand while lowering its left gripper around blue_mug_1. The mug remains upright on placemat_2, and the fingers are adjacent to its outer wall and handle region. The robot's torso is centered above the table, with its support column behind divided_serving_dish_1. food_pieces_1 remain in the dish's right-hand section, and spoon_1 lies to its left. dark_shaker_1 and dark_shaker_2 remain upright in the foreground-right. dinner_plate_1 with salad_1, fork_1, knife_1, and napkin_1 is partly visible at the lower left on placemat_1. dinner_plate_2 and placemat_3 are partly cropped. dining_chair_1 is mostly off the left edge; dining_chair_2 and dining_chair_3 remain behind the right side of the table. The glasses are about a forearm-length from the mug and do not touch it. Background cabinetry, wooden kitchen counters, microwave_1, kitchen_island_1, and kitchen_door_1 remain stationary; cutting boards and countertop containers are visible but not sharply resolved. Refrigerator, dishwasher and racks, oven, stovetop, hood, cookware, shelves, plants, bottles, coffee machine, framed picture, and oven towel cannot all be individually assessed from this framing.",
      "Frame 13: robot_1's left gripper settles more closely around blue_mug_1, which still rests upright on dining_table_1. Its fingers wrap around the mug's side while the palm hovers just above the rim level. The right hand holds wine_glass_1 and wine_glass_2 together without visible change in separation. Both glasses remain clear of the tabletop. divided_serving_dish_1, food_pieces_1, and spoon_1 remain on placemat_2 immediately left of the mug. dark_shaker_1 and dark_shaker_2 remain near the lower-right edge. dinner_plate_1 and salad_1 sit on placemat_1 at the left, with fork_1, knife_1, and folded napkin_1 nearby; dinner_plate_2 and placemat_3 are largely cropped. dining_chair_2 and dining_chair_3 line the far/right table side, while dining_chair_1 is mostly outside the frame. The robot's support column is directly behind the serving dish, separated from it by the table edge. Pale upper and lower kitchen cabinets, wooden counters, microwave_1, kitchen_island_1, and the closed-looking kitchen_door_1 are visible behind. The dishwasher assembly, refrigerator, cooking appliances, cookware, and finer countertop accessories are not sufficiently exposed to describe their states individually.",
      "Frame 14: robot_1's left fingers visibly enclose blue_mug_1 while the mug remains at table level. The wrist aligns more vertically above the mug, and the gripper is in direct contact with its side. wine_glass_1 and wine_glass_2 remain supported together in the opposite hand, several glass-foot widths above dining_table_1. divided_serving_dish_1 stays on placemat_2 beneath the robot's central support, with food_pieces_1 in the right section; spoon_1 remains to the left. dark_shaker_1 and dark_shaker_2 remain untouched in the foreground-right. dinner_plate_1, salad_1, fork_1, knife_1, napkin_1, and placemat_1 remain partly visible on the left. dinner_plate_2 and placemat_3 are cropped, and dining_chair_2 and dining_chair_3 remain behind the robot's left arm. dining_chair_1 is largely off-screen. No tableware other than the glasses and mug is contacted. The same background cabinets, counters, microwave, island, and kitchen door remain visible. dishwasher_1, dishwasher_door_1, dishwasher_upper_rack_1, dishwasher_lower_rack_1, refrigerator_1, oven_1, stovetop_1, range_hood_1, saucepan_1, frying_pan_1, and the small named accessories are outside the useful view or too soft to assess.",
      "Frame 15: robot_1 lifts blue_mug_1 from dining_table_1 with its left hand. A clear gap opens between the mug's bottom and placemat_2, while the mug remains upright. Its left elbow bends slightly outward. The right hand continues holding wine_glass_1 and wine_glass_2 together at the other side of its torso. divided_serving_dish_1, food_pieces_1, and spoon_1 remain below, with no visible displacement. dark_shaker_1 and dark_shaker_2 stay upright near the right foreground edge. dinner_plate_1 with salad_1 and its fork_1, knife_1, napkin_1, and placemat_1 remains at the left edge; dinner_plate_2 and placemat_3 are mostly cropped. dining_chair_2 and dining_chair_3 remain behind the lifted mug, and dining_chair_1 is largely outside the shot. The mug is roughly one mug-height above the table by this stage, whereas the paired glass feet are higher and farther left. The background remains pale upper and lower cabinets, wooden counters, microwave_1, kitchen_island_1, and kitchen_door_1. The dishwasher, refrigerator, cooking appliances, cookware, shelving, plants, bottles, coffee equipment, framed picture, cutting boards, knife block, and utensil holder are not all individually resolvable.",
      "Frame 16: robot_1 raises blue_mug_1 farther, bringing it toward lower-torso height with the left elbow bent. The mug is upright and firmly enclosed by the gripper. wine_glass_1 and wine_glass_2 remain in the right hand, their feet hanging just below the wrist and their bowls close together. Both held loads are now well clear of dining_table_1 and separated laterally by approximately the robot's torso width. divided_serving_dish_1 and food_pieces_1 remain on placemat_2, with spoon_1 beside them. dark_shaker_1 and dark_shaker_2 remain in the near-right foreground. dinner_plate_1, salad_1, fork_1, knife_1, napkin_1, and placemat_1 remain partially visible at lower left; dinner_plate_2 and placemat_3 are cropped. The wooden backs of dining_chair_2 and dining_chair_3 are visible beyond the mug, while dining_chair_1 is outside the crop. Upper and lower cabinets, wooden counters, microwave_1, kitchen_island_1, and kitchen_door_1 remain stationary in the background. The dishwasher assembly, refrigerator, oven, stovetop, hood, cookware, and other small kitchen objects are not sufficiently visible for individual current-state observations.",
      "Frame 17: robot_1 straightens its upper posture while holding blue_mug_1 in its bent left arm and wine_glass_1 and wine_glass_2 in its right gripper. The mug is near the lower edge of the torso and the glasses are slightly lower on the opposite side. Neither hand contacts dining_table_1. More of the robot's head and dark cap are visible, with its face oriented generally forward. divided_serving_dish_1, food_pieces_1, spoon_1, and placemat_2 remain at the bottom edge. The salad plate setting, including dinner_plate_1, salad_1, fork_1, knife_1, napkin_1, and placemat_1, is mostly cropped; dinner_plate_2, placemat_3, and the shakers are also near or beyond the lower boundary. dining_chair_2 and dining_chair_3 remain visible behind the left arm, and dining_chair_1 is out of view. The background includes kitchen_island_1, pale upper_kitchen_cabinets_1 and lower_kitchen_cabinets_1, wooden kitchen counter surfaces, microwave_1, and kitchen_door_1. Small countertop items remain indistinct. dishwasher_1, its door and racks, refrigerator_1, oven_1, stovetop_1, range_hood_1, cookware, and the remaining named accessories cannot be reliably evaluated in this framing.",
      "Frame 18: robot_1 remains centered in a frontal view, with blue_mug_1 upright in its left gripper and the two wine glasses gathered in its right gripper. Both elbows are bent, placing the objects beside and below the torso. The glasses' stems and feet remain clear of surrounding surfaces, and the mug is approximately a torso-width from them. The robot's head faces forward; no object release is visible. dining_table_1 is largely below the frame, so placemat_1, placemat_2, placemat_3, dinner_plate_1, dinner_plate_2, divided_serving_dish_1, napkin_1, fork_1, knife_1, spoon_1, salad_1, food_pieces_1, dark_shaker_1, and dark_shaker_2 are no longer clearly assessable. dining_chair_2 and dining_chair_3 remain visible at right, while dining_chair_1 is outside the crop. Behind the robot are upper and lower cabinets, wooden counter surfaces, microwave_1, kitchen_island_1, and kitchen_door_1. Plants and countertop objects are soft silhouettes rather than individually readable items. The dishwasher, its door and both racks, refrigerator, cooking appliances, cookware, wall shelves, bottles, framed picture, coffee machine, knife block, cutting boards, utensils, and oven towel are not adequately shown.",
      "Frame 19: A wide kitchen view shows robot_1 on its rectangular mobile base in front of dishwasher_1, immediately right of refrigerator_1. The robot's right arm extends down toward the upper edge of dishwasher_door_1, which is partly open and slopes diagonally from the appliance toward the robot. A blue object consistent with blue_mug_1 is visible near that hand; the glass pair is not individually resolved near the other bent arm. Both dishwasher racks remain mostly inside or obscured. refrigerator_1 is closed at left. microwave_1 sits on kitchen_counter_1, with bottle_1, bottle_2, and potted_plant_1 grouped farther left. upper_kitchen_cabinets_1 and lower_kitchen_cabinets_1 surround the workspace with closed-looking fronts. oven_1 is closed, oven_towel_1 hangs from its handle, and stovetop_1 supports cookware consistent with saucepan_1 and frying_pan_1 beneath range_hood_1. cutting_board_1, cutting_board_2, knife_block_1, utensil_holder_1, and cooking_utensils_1 are arranged along the rear counter. kitchen_counter_2 and kitchen_island_1 extend along the right; coffee_machine_1 and potted_plant_2 are farther right. wall_shelf_1 and wall_shelf_2 hold small objects near the refrigerator. framed_picture_1 is partly visible at the far right. Dining objects and kitchen_door_1 are outside this shot; only a chair/table edge appears in the foreground.",
      "Frame 20: robot_1 lowers its right hand along with dishwasher_door_1, which opens farther downward and is now less steeply inclined. The robot remains immediately in front of dishwasher_1, its base within roughly one base-width of the appliance opening. Its left arm stays bent near the torso; wine_glass_1 and wine_glass_2 are not separately distinguishable at this scale. blue_mug_1 appears near the lowered right hand but is partly obscured. dishwasher_upper_rack_1 and dishwasher_lower_rack_1 remain mostly concealed inside the appliance. refrigerator_1 stays closed at left; microwave_1 remains on kitchen_counter_1. bottle_1, bottle_2, potted_plant_1, wall_shelf_1, and wall_shelf_2 remain beside and above that counter. The upper and lower kitchen cabinet fronts remain stationary. oven_1 is closed with oven_towel_1 on its handle; saucepan_1 and frying_pan_1 remain on stovetop_1 under range_hood_1. cutting_board_1, cutting_board_2, knife_block_1, utensil_holder_1, and cooking_utensils_1 stay along the rear workspace. kitchen_counter_2, kitchen_island_1, coffee_machine_1, potted_plant_2, and the partly cropped framed_picture_1 remain to the right. Dining settings, shakers, and kitchen_door_1 are outside the view. No movement of the background kitchen objects is visible.",
      "Frame 21: robot_1's torso descends on its vertical support as the right hand follows dishwasher_door_1 farther downward. The door is now at a shallow diagonal above the floor, with its outer edge near the robot's lower body. The robot's head and shoulders sit lower relative to kitchen_counter_1 than in the preceding frame. dishwasher_1's dark opening is more exposed, although dishwasher_upper_rack_1 and dishwasher_lower_rack_1 are not clearly extended. The held glasses and blue_mug_1 are obscured by distance, arm position, and the door. refrigerator_1 remains closed. microwave_1, bottle_1, bottle_2, potted_plant_1, and the two wall shelves remain on the left side. upper_kitchen_cabinets_1 and lower_kitchen_cabinets_1 remain shut-looking. oven_1, oven_towel_1, stovetop_1, range_hood_1, saucepan_1, and frying_pan_1 retain their positions at center-right. cutting_board_1, cutting_board_2, knife_block_1, utensil_holder_1, and cooking_utensils_1 remain on the rear counter. kitchen_counter_2, kitchen_island_1, coffee_machine_1, potted_plant_2, and framed_picture_1 remain on the right. dining_table_1 and a chair edge are only marginally visible in the foreground; the table settings and kitchen_door_1 are out of frame.",
      "Frame 22: robot_1 lowers its upper assembly farther, bending both arms near the now nearly horizontal dishwasher_door_1. The door's outer edge is only slightly above its final flat position. The robot's base stays directly beside the opened area, and its right gripper remains close to the door edge. dishwasher_1's interior is dark; the upper and lower racks are not yet clearly presented outside the cavity. wine_glass_1, wine_glass_2, and blue_mug_1 cannot be individually located with confidence in this wide frame. refrigerator_1 remains closed, while microwave_1 and the left-counter bottles and potted_plant_1 remain stationary. wall_shelf_1 and wall_shelf_2 are visible above. Closed-looking upper and lower cabinets surround the counters. oven_1 stays closed with oven_towel_1 hanging down; saucepan_1 and frying_pan_1 remain on stovetop_1 beneath range_hood_1. The two cutting boards, knife_block_1, utensil_holder_1, and cooking_utensils_1 remain upright along the back counter. kitchen_counter_2, kitchen_island_1, coffee_machine_1, potted_plant_2, and framed_picture_1 remain visible at the right. Dining plates, placemats, cutlery, food, mug setting, shakers, and kitchen_door_1 are outside the useful view.",
      "Frame 23: dishwasher_door_1 is fully lowered or very close to horizontal, extending from dishwasher_1 toward robot_1 above the floor. The robot's torso is at its lowest visible position in this sequence, with its arms bent near the open appliance and the vertical support shortened above the base. The right hand is near the door's outer region; no separate placement of wine_glass_1, wine_glass_2, or blue_mug_1 is clearly visible. dishwasher_upper_rack_1 and dishwasher_lower_rack_1 remain dark and only partly exposed. The mobile base is adjacent to the door but does not visibly rest on it. refrigerator_1 remains closed. microwave_1, bottle_1, bottle_2, potted_plant_1, and the two wall shelves remain at left. Upper and lower cabinetry and both kitchen counters remain unchanged. oven_1 is closed with oven_towel_1 on its handle; saucepan_1 and frying_pan_1 remain on stovetop_1 under range_hood_1. cutting_board_1, cutting_board_2, knife_block_1, utensil_holder_1, and cooking_utensils_1 stay on the rear counter. kitchen_island_1, coffee_machine_1, potted_plant_2, and framed_picture_1 remain to the right. Dining objects and kitchen_door_1 remain outside this wide kitchen crop.",
      "Frame 24: The view changes to a wider side angle. robot_1 stands immediately right of open dishwasher_1, facing left with its upper body raised again. dishwasher_door_1 lies horizontal, and both dishwasher_upper_rack_1 and dishwasher_lower_rack_1 are extended into the aisle. The lower rack contains upright pale plates, but these cannot confidently be identified as dinner_plate_1 or dinner_plate_2. The robot extends both forearms over the upper rack; the wine glasses are clustered near its hands, although their individual contours are small. blue_mug_1 is not clearly resolved. A small green light is visible near the robot's base. refrigerator_1 stands closed at left; microwave_1 sits on kitchen_counter_1 beside potted_plant_1 and bottle_1/bottle_2. knife_block_1, cutting_board_1, cutting_board_2, utensil_holder_1, and cooking_utensils_1 line the rear workspace. oven_1 remains closed with oven_towel_1 hanging from it, and saucepan_1 and frying_pan_1 rest on stovetop_1 beneath range_hood_1. kitchen_counter_2 and kitchen_island_1 occupy the right, with coffee_machine_1, potted_plant_2, and framed_picture_1 visible above. Cabinet fronts remain closed-looking. The wall shelves are partly cropped. dining_table_1 and a chair back appear in the lower-right foreground; the remaining dining objects and kitchen_door_1 are outside the shot.",
      "Frame 25: robot_1 leans slightly toward dishwasher_upper_rack_1 and advances its hands over the rack's right side. wine_glass_1 and wine_glass_2 are near the grippers, with their stems and bowls beginning to angle downward toward the rack; exact finger contacts are difficult to separate at this scale. The robot is within arm's reach of dishwasher_1, its base just right of the horizontal dishwasher_door_1. dishwasher_lower_rack_1 remains extended beneath the upper rack and holds upright plates of uncertain identity. blue_mug_1 is not clearly distinguishable. refrigerator_1 remains closed, and microwave_1, bottle_1, bottle_2, potted_plant_1, and the partly visible wall shelves remain unchanged at left. upper_kitchen_cabinets_1 and lower_kitchen_cabinets_1 have stationary, closed-looking fronts. cutting_board_1, cutting_board_2, knife_block_1, utensil_holder_1, and cooking_utensils_1 remain along kitchen_counter_1. oven_1, oven_towel_1, stovetop_1, range_hood_1, saucepan_1, and frying_pan_1 remain behind the robot. kitchen_counter_2, kitchen_island_1, coffee_machine_1, potted_plant_2, and framed_picture_1 stay at right. Only the edge of dining_table_1 and one chair back are visible; individual dining chairs, settings, food, shakers, and kitchen_door_1 are not assessable.",
      "Frame 26: robot_1 extends its forearms farther left and lowers the wine glasses toward dishwasher_upper_rack_1. Its head angles downward toward the area immediately below the hands. wine_glass_1 and wine_glass_2 remain close together and are now positioned directly over the rack rather than beside it; their orientation is increasingly inverted, though the wide view obscures precise contact. dishwasher_door_1 remains horizontal, and dishwasher_lower_rack_1 remains extended with pale plates standing between its wires. blue_mug_1 is concealed among the upper-rack contents or by the hands. The robot's base remains beside the open appliance with little observable translation. refrigerator_1, microwave_1, kitchen_counter_1, bottle_1, bottle_2, potted_plant_1, and the partially cropped wall shelves remain unchanged. Upper and lower cabinets remain closed-looking. The cutting boards, knife block, utensil holder, and cooking utensils stay against the back wall. oven_1 remains closed with oven_towel_1 hanging; saucepan_1 and frying_pan_1 remain on stovetop_1 under range_hood_1. kitchen_counter_2, kitchen_island_1, coffee_machine_1, potted_plant_2, and framed_picture_1 remain visible at right. Dining settings, the three individually designated chairs, and kitchen_door_1 are not clearly shown.",
      "Frame 27: robot_1 bends farther forward at its upper assembly while lowering its hands into the upper-rack area. wine_glass_1 and wine_glass_2 are immediately above or partly between the wires of dishwasher_upper_rack_1, with the hand close to their raised stem/foot regions. The robot's elbows remain extended toward the appliance, and its head is tilted down. dishwasher_1 remains open, dishwasher_door_1 horizontal, and dishwasher_lower_rack_1 extended below with upright pale dishes of uncertain identity. blue_mug_1 is not separately resolved in this wide view. The robot's base stays to the right of the door, approximately one arm-length from the rack's inner region. refrigerator_1 remains closed; microwave_1, bottles, potted_plant_1, and wall shelves remain at left. Cabinet fronts and both wooden counters remain stationary. cutting_board_1, cutting_board_2, knife_block_1, utensil_holder_1, and cooking_utensils_1 remain at the back. oven_1, oven_towel_1, stovetop_1, range_hood_1, saucepan_1, and frying_pan_1 show no visible changes. kitchen_island_1, coffee_machine_1, potted_plant_2, and framed_picture_1 remain on the right. dining_table_1 and a chair edge are foreground fragments; placemats, cutlery, food, shakers, and kitchen_door_1 are not visible.",
      "Frame 28: robot_1 maintains a forward lean and lowers its hand a little farther toward dishwasher_upper_rack_1. The paired wine glasses are now largely aligned with the rack interior; their bowls are difficult to distinguish against the wires, while the gripper remains near their upper stem/foot area. No clear withdrawal of the hand is yet visible. dishwasher_door_1 and dishwasher_lower_rack_1 remain fully open and extended. The lower rack's pale plates stay upright, and blue_mug_1 is obscured at this distance. The robot's mobile base remains stationary beside the door, with the upper body leaning over the rack. refrigerator_1 remains closed. microwave_1, bottle_1, bottle_2, potted_plant_1, wall_shelf_1, and wall_shelf_2 remain along the left side. Upper and lower cabinets, kitchen_counter_1, and kitchen_counter_2 remain unchanged. The two cutting boards, knife block, utensil holder, and cooking utensils remain on the rear worktop. oven_1 is closed with oven_towel_1 hanging, and saucepan_1/frying_pan_1 remain on stovetop_1 beneath range_hood_1. kitchen_island_1, coffee_machine_1, potted_plant_2, and framed_picture_1 remain visible at right. Most dining objects, the individual chair identities, and kitchen_door_1 are outside the frame.",
      "Frame 29: A close-up shows dishwasher_upper_rack_1 with wine_glass_1 inverted on the left and wine_glass_2 inverted immediately to its right. Their bowls sit low among the wire dividers, their stems point upward, and their circular feet are above a dark horizontal support. robot_1's white gripper is directly above wine_glass_2, overlapping its stem/foot region; contact with the right glass appears to remain, while the left glass is unsupported by any clearly visible finger. blue_mug_1 is already inverted in the rack's lower-left foreground; its movement into this position was not clearly shown. The glasses are separated by only a narrow gap between their bowls. Dark fittings and other indistinct rack contents occupy the left side. dishwasher_1's cavity is partly visible behind the rack, but dishwasher_door_1 and dishwasher_lower_rack_1 are outside the close crop. Pale lower_kitchen_cabinets_1 with horizontal metal handles form the background. The robot's torso, head, base, and other arm are not visible. dining_table_1, all dining chairs and settings, refrigerator_1, microwave_1, oven_1, stovetop_1, range_hood_1, cookware, island, counters, upper cabinets, oven towel, cutting boards, knife block, utensils, coffee machine, plants, bottles, shelves, framed picture, and kitchen door are outside this close view.",
      "Frame 30: robot_1's gripper shifts slightly upward above wine_glass_2 while remaining immediately adjacent to its raised stem and foot. wine_glass_1 and wine_glass_2 stay inverted and side by side inside dishwasher_upper_rack_1, with their bowls supported between rack wires. The right glass appears slightly farther right than before, increasing the narrow separation between the two bowls. The left glass's circular foot remains clearly visible above the dark support rail. blue_mug_1 remains inverted at the lower left, partly hidden by rack wires; no movement of the mug is apparent. The hand-to-glass clearance is still small enough that complete release is uncertain. dishwasher_1's dark interior and rack fixtures remain at left, while dishwasher_door_1 and dishwasher_lower_rack_1 are outside the crop. Pale lower_kitchen_cabinets_1 remain behind the rack. The remainder of robot_1 and all dining-table objects, including the plates, placemats, salad, food pieces, cutlery, napkin, divided dish, shakers, and chairs, are not visible. Refrigerator, microwave, oven, stovetop, hood, cookware, counters, island, upper cabinets, oven towel, cutting boards, knife block, utensil holder and utensils, coffee machine, plants, bottles, shelves, framed picture, and kitchen door are likewise outside the frame.",
      "Frame 31: robot_1 raises and slightly opens its gripper above the right-hand inverted wine_glass_2. The lower finger edge is now above the glass's stem support region, although overlap still prevents a definitive view of full separation. wine_glass_1 remains inverted at left, and wine_glass_2 remains inverted at right, both with bowls low in dishwasher_upper_rack_1 and feet high above the rack. Their positions appear stable relative to the wire dividers. blue_mug_1 stays inverted in the lower-left foreground, several rack-wire intervals left of the glasses. The dark horizontal stem-support fitting runs behind both upward-pointing stems. dishwasher_1 is only partly represented by the dark opening and rack structure; dishwasher_door_1 and dishwasher_lower_rack_1 are not shown. lower_kitchen_cabinets_1 remain in the background. The robot's body and mobile base are outside the crop. dining_table_1, dining_chair_1, dining_chair_2, dining_chair_3, all placemats, plates, food, cutlery, napkin, divided serving dish, and shakers are absent from view. The refrigerator, microwave, cooking appliances, cookware, kitchen island and counters, upper cabinets, towel, boards, knife block, utensils, coffee machine, plants, bottles, shelves, framed picture, and kitchen door cannot be assessed here.",
      "Frame 32: robot_1's partially open gripper remains just above and to the right of wine_glass_2's upward-pointing stem/foot area. Its lower finger is marginally farther from the glass than earlier, but the exact final contact state remains visually ambiguous. wine_glass_1 stands inverted at left and wine_glass_2 inverted at right in dishwasher_upper_rack_1; both bowls remain nested between the wire dividers without visible displacement. Their feet project above the dark stem-support rail, and the right glass appears slightly taller in the image. blue_mug_1 remains inverted in the lower-left rack area. The rack itself stays extended and stationary in this close framing. dishwasher_1's dark interior is only partly visible; dishwasher_door_1 and dishwasher_lower_rack_1 are outside the crop. lower_kitchen_cabinets_1 with metal handles remain behind the hand and glasses. The robot's head, torso, other arm, support column, and base are not visible. All dining furniture, plates, placemats, utensils, napkin, salad, serving dish, food pieces, and shakers are outside the frame. Refrigerator, microwave, oven, stovetop, hood, cookware, island, counters, upper cabinets, oven towel, cutting boards, knife block, utensil holder and utensils, coffee machine, plants, bottles, wall shelves, framed picture, and kitchen door likewise have no directly observable state in this final close-up."
