      "Frame 01: robot_01 is centered in terrain_01, with its white body between angular terrain_02 boulders and the steep terrain_03 slab immediately to its left. Its wheels are supported at unequal elevations, with the nearer legs extending down onto the lower rock surface. The nearest slab is less than one robot body length away; other rocks surround it within roughly one to three body lengths. overlay_01 spreads beneath the wheels and forward across the rock, becoming visually compressed on steep faces. Motion cannot be established from this frame alone. Portions of walkway_01 and background_03 appear beyond the rocks, while background_01 towers and background_02 pillar arrays occupy the distance. target_01\u201304 are not visible. platform_01\u201304, pit_01\u201304, bridge_01, and obstacle_01 are not individually identifiable from this initial angle.",
      "Frame 02: robot_01 has advanced through the rocky corridor, but a tall foreground slab now obscures much of its left and central body. Its visible right-side legs and wheels remain close to the rock surface. The camera has shifted laterally, bringing a large terrain_02 boulder to the left of the robot and more stepped terrain_03 surfaces into view on the right. Clearances to the adjacent rocks are less than approximately one body length. overlay_01 extends around the occluding slab and across the uneven ground. terrain_01 remains the immediate support area. walkway_01 and the static background_01\u201303 structures remain farther away. None of target_01\u201304 is clearly visible; platform_01\u201304, their corresponding pit_01\u201304, bridge_01, and obstacle_01 remain outside the clearly identifiable portion of the scene.",
      "Frame 03: robot_01 emerges from behind the foreground slab and is more fully visible beside a large faceted terrain_02 boulder on its left. Its chassis pitches diagonally as the articulated legs span uneven terrain_03 surfaces, with the lower wheels extending down the slope. It moves through a gap only about one body width wider than the robot itself. overlay_01 covers the rock under its wheels and the open patch immediately ahead. terrain_01 continues across the foreground, while broad walkway_01 surfaces lie beyond the rocky section. background_01 towers, background_02 pillar arrangements, and background_03 elevated structures remain stationary in the distance. target_01\u201304 are not discernible. The isolated platform_01\u201304 and associated pit_01\u201304, bridge_01, and obstacle_01 are not yet individually resolved.",
      "Frame 04: robot_01 travels around the upper-right side of the prominent foreground boulder. Its white chassis appears closer to horizontal, although the legs remain bent at different angles over the broken terrain_03 slabs. A smaller pointed terrain_02 rock lies immediately to its left, within roughly half a body length, and a stepped rock face lies about one body length to its right. The large foreground boulder partially blocks the lower wheels. overlay_01 remains centered around the robot and extends onto the rocks ahead. terrain_01 still surrounds the robot; walkway_01 is visible farther beyond it. background_01\u201303 remain unchanged apart from camera parallax. target_01\u201304 and the individually specified platform_01\u201304, pit_01\u201304, bridge_01, and obstacle_01 are not clearly visible.",
      "Frame 05: robot_01 crosses a comparatively open rocky patch between a low, layered terrain_03 slab ahead-left and a pointed terrain_02 boulder immediately below-right. The chassis is nearly level, with the wheeled legs spread across small height differences. The nearest rocks are within approximately one body length. The camera pulls the wider edge of terrain_01 into view, exposing dark recessed space to the left and broad walkway_01 surfaces beyond the rocks. overlay_01 forms several cyan patches across the differently angled surfaces around the robot. background_01 blocks, background_02 narrow-pillar arrays, and background_03 elevated structures remain distant and stationary. No target sphere is clearly visible yet; platform_01\u201304, pit_01\u201304, bridge_01, and obstacle_01 cannot all be individually distinguished.",
      "Frame 06: robot_01 moves onto a downward-sloping terrain_03 section and becomes visibly tilted, with its body angled across the slope and its legs extending unevenly. A large terrain_02 boulder remains very close on its right, while lower rock slabs open to its left. overlay_01 stretches down the incline beneath it. target_01 first appears at the far-left edge as a yellow sphere above platform_01, several robot body lengths away across pit_01. Only part of that isolated square platform and its surrounding recess is visible. walkway_01 borders the area beyond terrain_01. target_02\u201304, platform_02\u201304, pit_02\u201304, bridge_01, and obstacle_01 are not identifiable here. background_01\u201303 remain visible beyond the immediate obstacle area.",
      "Frame 07: robot_01 continues down the sloping terrain_03 slabs, its chassis noticeably canted and its lower wheels reaching toward the next rock surface. It remains within about half a body length of the faceted terrain_02 rock to its right. target_01 and more of platform_01 are now visible on the left, separated from the robot by several body lengths and the dark gap of pit_01. The sphere remains suspended above the platform with a small offset shadow. overlay_01 extends down the rocky slope toward the platform-facing edge of terrain_01. walkway_01 forms broad gray boundaries around the recess. target_02\u201304, platform_02\u201304, pit_02\u201304, bridge_01, and obstacle_01 remain outside the identifiable view. background_01\u201303 stay stationary.",
      "Frame 08: robot_01 descends onto a lower, more open terrain_03 slab at the edge of terrain_01. Its body straightens somewhat, and the legs spread with two visible wheels near the slab's descending edge. A large terrain_02 boulder is now behind-right, approximately one body length away. platform_01 lies left of the robot across pit_01, with target_01 hovering over its top roughly three to four projected body lengths away. overlay_01 follows the slope beneath the robot and extends toward the dark gap. walkway_01 is visible behind platform_01 and beyond the rocky area. The other target_02\u201304, platform_02\u201304, pit_02\u201304, bridge_01, and obstacle_01 remain unidentifiable. background_01\u201303 retain their distant arrangement.",
      "Frame 09: robot_01 reaches the outer edge of the sloping terrain_03 surface and extends outward toward platform_01. Its chassis is nearly horizontal, with the leading legs projecting over pit_01 and the trailing wheels still close to the rocky edge. target_01 remains over the left-hand square platform, now only a few body lengths away. The near edge of platform_01 is approximately one to two projected body lengths from the robot. terrain_02 boulders recede to its right, and terrain_01 no longer surrounds it on all sides. overlay_01 covers the launch-side rock and partly overlaps the dark recessed area in the view. walkway_01 and background_01\u201303 remain visible. The later platforms, targets, pits, bridge_01, and obstacle_01 remain outside clear identification.",
      "Frame 10: robot_01 is suspended over pit_01 between the rocky boundary and platform_01, with no clear wheel contact visible. Its chassis has rotated into a steep diagonal, and its articulated legs extend above and below the body. The square platform is to its left, within roughly one body length of the nearer wheels, while target_01 remains above the platform farther left. terrain_01\u201303 rise along the right-hand edge of the view, now behind the crossing motion. overlay_01 appears on the lower visible surfaces beneath the robot rather than as a flat patch directly supporting it. walkway_01 borders the recess in the background. target_02\u201304, platform_02\u201304, pit_02\u201304, bridge_01, and obstacle_01 are not clearly resolved; background_01\u201303 remain stationary.",
      "Frame 11: robot_01 reaches the near-right edge of platform_01 with its chassis still pitched upward relative to the platform top. Its forward portion overlaps the top surface while two extended wheels remain above pit_01 near the vertical side face. The gap between the robot and platform is effectively closed at the leading end, although full four-wheel support is not yet visually clear. target_01 is still visible above the farther-left portion of platform_01, about two projected body lengths away. overlay_01 spans the platform top and the adjacent rocky-side surface. terrain_01\u201303 are mostly at the right margin, while walkway_01 and background_01\u201303 frame the scene. The later target/platform/pit groups, bridge_01, and obstacle_01 remain indistinct.",
      "Frame 12: robot_01 is now on top of platform_01, with the body approximately level and its wheeled legs positioned over the square surface. It sits in the central-to-right portion, roughly one body length from the nearest visible edge. target_01 is no longer visible above this platform. pit_01 surrounds the square as a dark blue-gray channel, and walkway_01 forms the outer border. target_02 appears far in the upper-right view above platform_02, several platform widths from the robot; pit_02 is partially discernible around it. overlay_01 forms a broad cyan patch on platform_01. terrain_01\u201303 have moved mostly out of view. target_03\u201304, platform_03\u201304, pit_03\u201304, bridge_01, and obstacle_01 remain outside clear identification. background_01\u201303 remain visible.",
      "Frame 13: robot_01 moves across platform_01 and begins changing its body heading, with the chassis angled diagonally relative to the square's edges. Its wheels remain over the platform top, and the articulated legs show different bends during the turn. The nearest edge is around one body length away. target_01 remains absent from view. target_02 is still visible on the distant upper-right platform_02, separated by walkway_01 and pit_02. pit_01 remains immediately around the robot's platform. overlay_01 rotates and shifts with the robot, spreading across the near-left portion of platform_01. terrain_01\u201303 are mostly outside the frame, as are target_03\u201304, platform_03\u201304, pit_03\u201304, bridge_01, and obstacle_01. background_01\u201303 remain stationary.",
      "Frame 14: robot_01 continues pivoting on platform_01, presenting a more end-on view of the chassis. Its four legs are spread in a compact stance, with the wheels remaining on or very close to the top surface. The robot is near the upper-left half of the platform, approximately one body length from the nearest pit_01 edge. overlay_01 is centered beneath the turning body. target_01 is not visible; target_02 remains a small yellow sphere over the distant platform_02, with pit_02 and walkway_01 separating that location from the robot. No displacement is visible in the fixed structures. terrain_01\u201303 and the target_03\u201304/platform_03\u201304/pit_03\u201304 group, bridge_01, and obstacle_01 are outside clear view. background_01\u201303 continue across the distance.",
      "Frame 15: robot_01 has rotated farther and now stands diagonally across platform_01, with its body aligned toward the right-hand side of the frame. The leg stance opens slightly as it moves away from the previous pivot location. Its distance to the right-side edge is around one to two body lengths. overlay_01 shifts toward that side of the platform. target_01 remains absent. target_02 is visible above platform_02 in the upper-right background, still several body lengths away beyond walkway_01 and pit_02. pit_01 remains the immediate gap around platform_01. terrain_01\u201303 are largely outside the frame. target_03\u201304, platform_03\u201304, pit_03\u201304, bridge_01, and obstacle_01 are not individually visible; background_01\u201303 remain stationary.",
      "Frame 16: robot_01 approaches the right-hand edge of platform_01, lowering its chassis slightly and extending its legs toward the neighboring rocky-side boundary. The leading wheels are within about half a body length of the edge, with pit_01 immediately beyond. overlay_01 reaches the platform edge and partially extends toward the opposite surface. target_01 remains out of view. target_02 is visible farther ahead above platform_02, beyond the broad walkway_01 and pit_02. The shadowed terrain_01 boundary and angular terrain_02\u201303 surfaces re-enter along the right side, roughly one gap-width from the robot. target_03\u201304, platform_03\u201304, pit_03\u201304, bridge_01, and obstacle_01 remain unresolved. background_01\u201303 continue unchanged in the distance.",
      "Frame 17: robot_01 crosses off platform_01 toward the narrow rocky-side margin of pit_01. Its chassis is stretched nearly horizontally over the gap, with legs extended toward the receiving surface on the right. platform_01 falls behind-left, less than one body length from the trailing wheels. The receiving terrain_03 ledge is immediately under the leading end, while terrain_02 casts a large dark shadow over it. overlay_01 is concentrated on that receiving strip and nearby rock. target_01 remains absent. target_02 is visible over platform_02 farther ahead, beyond walkway_01 and pit_02. terrain_01 occupies the right boundary rather than the main route ahead. target_03\u201304, platform_03\u201304, pit_03\u201304, bridge_01, and obstacle_01 remain outside clear view; background_01\u201303 are stationary.",
      "Frame 18: robot_01 has reached the shadowed strip beside the rocks and moves forward along it. The white body is dimmed by shadow, with its wheels close to the narrow supporting surface between pit_01 on the left and a large projecting terrain_02 boulder on the right. Clearance beneath or beside the boulder is less than roughly one body length. terrain_03 slopes border the strip. platform_01 is mostly behind the camera, and target_01 remains absent. target_02 and platform_02 are visible ahead across the more open walkway_01, with pit_02 surrounding the square. overlay_01 conforms to the shadowed strip beneath the robot. target_03\u201304, platform_03\u201304, pit_03\u201304, bridge_01, and obstacle_01 remain unidentifiable. background_01\u201303 continue beyond.",
      "Frame 19: robot_01 advances out from beside the large terrain_02 boulder toward the open walkway_01. Its chassis is more upright and level, though still largely shadowed, with the wheels spread across the flat-to-sloped transition. The rocky terrain_01\u201303 is immediately behind-right, approximately one body length away. platform_02 and target_02 are now clearly ahead, several body lengths distant, inside the rectangular recess pit_02. platform_01 and pit_01 have receded out of the main view; target_01 is not visible. overlay_01 stretches from beneath the robot onto the brighter walkway ahead. target_03\u201304, platform_03\u201304, pit_03\u201304, bridge_01, and obstacle_01 remain outside identification. background_01 towers and background_02\u201303 obstacle structures remain fixed.",
      "Frame 20: robot_01 reaches the broad, brighter walkway_01 beside pit_02 and turns toward platform_02. Its body is near the recessed area's front-right corner, with the closest edge less than one body length away. target_02 hovers above the far portion of platform_02, approximately three to four projected body lengths from the robot. The square platform is surrounded by a continuous dark gap; its near edge is roughly one to two body lengths across that gap from the robot. overlay_01 lies primarily on the walkway beneath the turning chassis. terrain_01\u201303 are behind-right or out of view. target_01, platform_01, and pit_01 are no longer visible; the third and fourth target/platform/pit groups, bridge_01, and obstacle_01 remain unresolved. background_01\u201303 remain static.",
      "Frame 21: robot_01 moves up to the front lip of pit_02, facing the near edge of platform_02. Its chassis dips slightly and the legs become more compact, with the leading wheels close to the walkway boundary. The open gap is roughly a robot body length in projected width. target_02 remains suspended over the far half of the square, about two to three body lengths beyond the robot. overlay_01 forms a cyan patch on walkway_01 directly behind and beneath it. platform_02 and pit_02 dominate the view. terrain_01\u201303, platform_01, pit_01, and target_01 are out of view, as are the individually identifiable target_03\u201304, platform_03\u201304, pit_03\u201304, bridge_01, and obstacle_01. background_01\u201303 remain stationary.",
      "Frame 22: robot_01 traverses the near gap of pit_02 and reaches platform_02. Its chassis is angled upward, with the forward portion over the platform top and the lower wheels near the front vertical face. The leading end has closed the gap to the platform, while the trailing legs remain extended over the recess. target_02 is still visible above the far edge, roughly one to two body lengths from the chassis. overlay_01 now lies mostly on platform_02, extending ahead of the robot. walkway_01 borders the square recess behind and around it. Earlier terrain_01\u201303, platform_01, pit_01, and target_01 are offscreen. target_03\u201304, platform_03\u201304, pit_03\u201304, bridge_01, and obstacle_01 remain unresolved; background_01\u201303 are unchanged.",
      "Frame 23: robot_01 is supported on platform_02, with its chassis nearly level and its wheeled legs spread across the top. It occupies the central-to-far portion of the square, approximately one body length from the far edge. target_02 is no longer visible. overlay_01 forms a cyan footprint around and ahead of the robot. pit_02 remains a dark channel on three visible sides, and walkway_01 runs beyond the far edge. target_01 and the first platform/pit are outside the frame, along with terrain_01\u201303. target_03\u201304, platform_03\u201304, pit_03\u201304, bridge_01, and obstacle_01 are not yet individually distinguishable. background_01 towers are prominent behind the walkway, with background_02 pillar arrays and background_03 elevated obstacle surfaces farther away.",
      "Frame 24: robot_01 moves toward the right-hand edge of platform_02 and begins extending over pit_02 toward walkway_01. The chassis is nearly horizontal, with the leading legs projecting beyond the square and the rear wheels still close to its top edge. The receiving walkway is roughly one body length away in projection. target_02 remains absent. overlay_01 covers the departure edge and is visible on the neighboring surface across the gap. platform_02 occupies the lower-left portion of the frame as the camera follows the movement to the right. terrain_01\u201303, target_01, platform_01, and pit_01 are out of view. The third and fourth target/platform/pit groups, bridge_01, and obstacle_01 remain unidentifiable; background_01\u201303 retain their positions.",
      "Frame 25: robot_01 reaches walkway_01 on the right side of pit_02. Its front portion is over the broad flat surface, with the rear wheels close to the pit-side edge, and the chassis settles toward a level attitude. platform_02 is behind-left across the gap, approximately one body length from the nearest part of the robot. target_02 remains absent. overlay_01 spreads across the receiving walkway and extends rightward. A larger recessed region becomes visible on the right, but platform_03 and its target are not yet clearly shown in this frame. pit_03 is beginning to enter the view; bridge_01, platform_04, pit_04, obstacle_01, and target_03\u201304 remain unresolved. Earlier terrain and platform_01 are offscreen. background_01\u201303 remain stationary.",
      "Frame 26: robot_01 traverses walkway_01 to the lip of pit_03, with its body turning toward platform_03 on the right. The polygonal platform rises from the recess about one to two body lengths across the gap. target_03 is clearly visible as a large yellow sphere above its top, roughly two to three projected body lengths from the robot. The robot's leading wheels are close to the walkway edge, and overlay_01 lies under its compact turning stance. platform_02 and pit_02 are now behind-left or out of view; target_01\u201302 remain absent. bridge_01 is not yet fully exposed by this angle. platform_04, target_04, pit_04, and obstacle_01 are outside clear view. terrain_01\u201303 are offscreen; background_01\u201303 remain fixed.",
      "Frame 27: robot_01 has crossed onto platform_03, the broad polygonal top inside pit_03. Its chassis is slightly angled across the surface, and its four wheeled legs spread around the center-left area. target_03 is no longer visible. bridge_01 is now clearly exposed, extending as a narrow straight connection from the polygonal platform's right side to walkway_01. The bridge entrance is within approximately one body length of the robot, while the outer walkway lies several body lengths along the bridge. overlay_01 covers the platform top and reaches toward the bridge. target_01\u201302, platform_01\u201302, pit_01\u201302, and terrain_01\u201303 are offscreen. target_04, platform_04, pit_04, and obstacle_01 are not yet resolved. background_01\u201303 remain stationary.",
      "Frame 28: robot_01 advances from platform_03 onto bridge_01. The white chassis is aligned approximately with the bridge, and its wheels lie close to the narrow deck's side edges. The polygonal platform is immediately behind-left, while walkway_01 is about one to two body lengths ahead. pit_03 drops away on both sides of the bridge, emphasizing the limited lateral clearance. target_03 remains absent. overlay_01 forms a long cyan strip along the bridge and a wider patch on the walkway beyond. Earlier terrain_01\u201303, platform_01\u201302, pit_01\u201302, and target_01\u201302 are outside the frame. target_04, platform_04, pit_04, and obstacle_01 are not yet clearly visible. background_01 towers, background_02 arrays, and background_03 structures remain fixed.",
      "Frame 29: robot_01 reaches the walkway_01 end of bridge_01, with its leading wheels on the broad surface and its rear wheels near the bridge exit. platform_03 lies behind-left across pit_03, about two body lengths away. Ahead-right, obstacle_01 becomes visible as a row of separated narrow stepping pillars spanning pit_04 toward platform_04. target_04 hovers above that far square platform, several body lengths from the robot. The first stepping pillar is roughly two to three body lengths away along the walkway. overlay_01 spreads across the bridge exit and the adjacent turning area. target_03 remains absent; earlier targets, platforms, pits, and terrain_01\u201303 are outside the view. background_01\u201303 remain stationary, with dense pillar arrangements prominent farther back.",
      "Frame 30: robot_01 moves along walkway_01 to the start of obstacle_01 and turns to align with the stepping-pillar row. Its leading legs approach the first narrow pillar, within roughly half a body length, while the body remains mostly over the broad walkway. platform_04 is several body lengths ahead across pit_04, with target_04 visibly suspended above its top. The separated pillar tops provide much narrower support than the walkway, and dark gaps are visible between them. overlay_01 covers the approach area and reaches onto the first pillars. bridge_01, platform_03, and pit_03 recede behind-left; target_03 is absent. terrain_01\u201303 and the first two platform/pit groups are offscreen. background_01\u201303 remain fixed.",
      "Frame 31: robot_01 is partway across obstacle_01, spanning several narrow pillar tops above pit_04. Its chassis is low and nearly horizontal, while the articulated legs are placed at different positions along the separated supports. Some wheels appear close to the pillar edges, with visible unsupported gaps beneath the body. platform_04 is immediately ahead, approximately one body length from the chassis, and target_04 remains above its top slightly farther forward. overlay_01 appears across the pillar tops and the near portion of the receiving platform. walkway_01 is behind-left and around the outer recess. bridge_01, platform_03, pit_03, earlier platform/pit groups, and terrain_01\u201303 are outside the main view; target_01\u201303 are absent. background_01\u201303 remain stationary.",
      "Frame 32: robot_01 is now on platform_04, with its chassis diagonally oriented and its wheeled legs spread over the square top. It has moved beyond obstacle_01; the final stepping pillar is immediately behind-left, less than one body length from the rear of the robot. target_04 is no longer visible. overlay_01 forms a broad cyan dotted patch under the chassis and toward the platform's right edge. pit_04 surrounds the platform and remains visible beneath the pillar row. walkway_01 borders the recess farther left and behind, separated from the robot by the gap. terrain_01\u201303, platform_01\u201303, pit_01\u201303, bridge_01, and target_01\u201303 are outside this final view. background_01 towers, background_02 dense pillar fields, and background_03 elevated platforms and ramps remain stationary."
